`createBitReader` creates a reader over a byte array. Each reader must maintain its own cursor, independent of every other reader. `read(width)` consumes `width` bits in most-significant-bit-first order and returns them as an unsigned number. Callers provide widths from 1 through 32. If fewer than `width` bits remain, it returns `null` without advancing. `reset()` returns only that reader to the beginning.

Use only deterministic standard-language facilities. Do not access the filesystem, network, clock, or randomness, and do not use external packages.

